            {
              "id": "3346c328-504f-4e96-933b-42d4380b8cff",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Preludes: Essays on the Ludic Imagination, 1961-1981</strong></em> was written by Christine Downing, published by iUniverse, Inc., May 5, 2005."
            },
            {
              "id": "f4a6b510-ffdb-477b-a059-7c4b3532a14e",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "2ea63dfd-c102-4bb5-ab37-07a6983bb83a",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>These essays are clearly not about play as unseriousness, not about fun and games, a point that should be abundantly demonstrated by the reference to the death camps of the Holocaust. They are about the space, the Spielraum, necessary for the wheel of life to turn soulfully. Christine Downing's essays may be felt to function as a possible prelude to the play of a truly </em><a href=\"#/ludus\"><em>ludic</em></a><em> imagination, which, like Buber's &quot;slow medicine,&quot; quietly enters the soul, working into the heart, awakening a secret </em><a href=\"#/harmony\"><em>melody</em></a><em> to be noticed only later.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "fbda64af-e235-4ed1-873e-c50dc7b26a28",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
